<!DOCTYPE html>

<html>
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Deures" %></title>

    <%#
      The scale clamp backs up touch-action: none, and viewport-fit lets the shell paint under
      the home indicator while its padding keeps the screen clear of it.
    %>

    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover"
    >

    <meta name="application-name" content="Deures">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <%#
      The manifest link, the apple-touch-icon and the standalone meta tags belong to the install
      view alone: only that request holds the plaintext token the manifest and the icon behind it
      have to carry, and both answer for a child.
    %>
    <%= yield :head %>

    <%# The pad's click, fetched before the first key is pressed rather than on it. %>
    <link rel="preload" href="<%= asset_path "key.wav" %>" as="audio" type="audio/wav">

    <%#
      The rasters first and the SVG last: an SVG favicon carries its own prefers-color-scheme
      swap, so a browser that can adapt should prefer it, and one that cannot never reaches it.
    %>
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png" sizes="512x512">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon-32.png" type="image/png" sizes="32x32">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">

    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :app, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>

  <%#
    The overlay is rendered on every page and toggled with `hidden`, because the request that
    would fetch it on demand is the one that has just failed. It sits outside the yielded
    screen so that nothing a response swaps can take it, or the retry driving it, away.
  %>

  <body
    data-controller="connection"
    data-action="turbo:submit-start->connection#waiting
                     turbo:before-fetch-response->connection#inspect
                     turbo:submit-end->connection#settled"
  >
    <%= yield %>
    <%= render "shared/no_connection" %>
  </body>
</html>
